{% extends 'help/_layout.html.twig' %}
{% block help_title %}Inflammation Score{% endblock %}

{% block help_body %}
<figure class="figure d-block border rounded shadow-sm overflow-hidden mb-4 w-100">
    <img src="{{ asset('images/help/inflammation.png') }}" class="figure-img img-fluid mb-0 w-100"
         alt="The Insights & Trends overview, led by the daily inflammation-score tile">
</figure>
<p>The inflammation score is a daily estimate of how <strong>pro-inflammatory</strong> or
<strong>anti-inflammatory</strong> your food was, on a scale from −10 (strongly anti-inflammatory) to +10
(strongly pro-inflammatory). It's an educational wellness signal — <em>not</em> a medical measurement.</p>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">How it's calculated</h2>
<p>It's a transparent, rule-based estimate (no AI guesswork), blending two signals:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Nutrients</strong> — saturated fat, sugar, and sodium push the score up (more inflammatory);
        fiber and antioxidant vitamins (A, C, D, E, B-vitamins, plus magnesium, zinc, selenium) push it
        down.</li>
    <li><strong>Food types</strong> — items like processed meat, fried food, and sugary drinks nudge it up;
        fatty fish, olive oil, leafy greens, berries, and turmeric nudge it down.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Where to see it</h2>
<p>Today's score is a badge on your <a href="{{ path('app_help_show', {topic: 'dashboard'}) }}">Dashboard</a>.
Over time, <strong>Insights &amp; Trends</strong> charts it day by day, with colored points by band and a
tooltip breaking down what pushed each day up or down.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block help_related %}
<hr class="my-4">
